Article 13 (Handling of International Money Orders)
When an international money order arrives at an exchange post office, it shall be handled as follows:
1. For a card money order, the international money order certificate received shall be sent to the payee; for a list money order, an international money order certificate prepared on the basis of the list shall be sent to the payee;
2. For a deposit money order, the remittance details transmitted by the exchange post office of the country where the payee's account is held shall be received as a computer output and the amount shall be deposited into the payee's account;
3. The exchange post office shall register the arrival details of the international money order through a terminal and retain a computer output of the details.
